ows 14-16: RRRNNN (3 R's, 3 N's)\n- Rows 17-19: ONNN (1 O, 3 N's)\n- Rows 20-22: ONNNRRR (1 O, 3 N's, 3 R's)\n- Rows 23-25: ONNN (1 O, 3 N's)\n- Rows 26-28: ONNNRRR (1 O, 3 N's, 3 R's)\n- Rows 29-31: RRRONNN (3 R's, 1 O, 3 N's)\n- Rows 32-34: ONNNNNNNNNN (1 O, 11 N's)\nSo the green shape is a vertical \"E\" shape with the opening on the left.\nThe goal seems to be to position the white shape so that its opening aligns with the green shape's opening, or something like that.\nLet me try moving the white shape to overlap with the green shape and see what happens.\nActually, let me first try SPACE again to see if it rotates the white shape further.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "World model: SPACE rotates white shape. Currently horizontal at rows 11-19, cols 11-28. Green=90 at rows 14-34, cols 44-50.\nGoal model: Try SPACE again to rotate white shape further.\nPlan: Press SPACE to rotate white shape.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Try SPACE again to rotate white shape\nresult = action(['SPACE'])\n\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nwhite_nodes = [n for n in seg['nodes'] if n['color'] == 'W' and n['pixels'] > 50]\ngreen_pixels = sum(n['pixels'] for n in seg['nodes'] if n['color'] == 'N')\n\nprint(f\"Green pixels: {green_pixels}\")\nif white_nodes:\n    w = white_nodes[0]\n    boundary = w['boundary']\n    rows = [p[0] for p in boundary]\n    cols = [p[1] for p in boundary]\n    print(f\"White shape: rows {min(rows)}-{max(rows)}, cols {min(cols)}-{max(cols)}\")\n    print(f\"  Height: {max(rows) - min(rows) + 1}, Width: {max(cols) - min(cols) + 1}\")\n\nprint(\"Level completed:\", last_action_result.get('level_completed'))\nprint(\"Game over:\", last_action_result.get('game_over'))\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "Green pixels: 90